{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>For the skin of his face sent forth rays</b> — he merited the radiance of his face through 'I will draw you to Me' (משכותי כפי עליך). And some say: from the writing of the tablets he merited the radiance. 'קרנים מידו לו ושם חביון עוזו' — rashei tevot of לוח (tablet):"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The notarikon forms the word לוח from the initial letters of the phrase קרנים מידו לו ושם חביון עוזו. The phrase appears to be a poetic or liturgical line; its precise source is uncertain. The word משכותי is given here in the form found in the source text."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:06.768325945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}